{
  "content": {
    "arguments": "$ARGUMENTS",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "id": "3d32aedf-6ecc-4b6f-9e80-2db2442df689",
        "text": "Use the Bash tool. The Pebbles CLI at \"{PEBBLES_CLI}\" is the ONLY sanctioned way to change spec files — never edit .pebble files directly."
      },
      {
        "id": "10e319f3-f5e0-4bcd-9853-eaf720d986f3",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Spec mutation contract (rules/system/spec-mutation-contract)"
      },
      {
        "id": "c32eb613-a524-4320-9167-7b5f1aa71d30",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Table completeness (rules/system/table-completeness)"
      },
      {
        "id": "87858972-9e56-4bc2-9c90-c6e9e78a0ff8",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Reference integrity (rules/system/reference-integrity)"
      }
    ],
    "examples": [],
    "kind": "skill",
    "onFailure": [
      {
        "id": "b1588a57-6a22-4c60-9da0-c592fe148d7d",
        "text": "Read the CLI error — it names the fix; correct the call and retry once"
      },
      {
        "id": "b26da6fb-54d2-437a-9d29-64bd99ec06c2",
        "text": "NEVER fall back to editing .pebble files directly, whatever failed"
      },
      {
        "id": "325dbe6c-5150-4da7-8649-7dc747d8cfd2",
        "text": "If still blocked, report the exact command and error to the user and stop"
      }
    ],
    "output": "The created pebble's path and id (plus droppedRefs if links didn't resolve).",
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "id": "212206fd-8bf2-4e14-84e4-dd6d9ac836da",
        "text": "The pebble's SECTION/kind is classified (model vs structure vs contract vs workflow vs checklist) before creating"
      },
      {
        "id": "1e7c4f8d-9550-4e96-8de8-f585bd44754c",
        "text": "A query confirms no existing pebble already covers this topic"
      }
    ],
    "purpose": "Create a new pebble safely",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "c42c4e9b-266f-458f-bab8-82ba918bc871",
        "text": "Create a new pebble — classified correctly and complete: $ARGUMENTS"
      },
      {
        "id": "9c2c67a3-fb54-4e8e-af05-d1f5780e55d4",
        "text": "STEP 0 — CLASSIFY (the load-bearing decision): persisted DB table → models (DB semantics: PK/refKey/NOT NULL/defaults) · in-code shape (DTO/payload/config/return type) → structures (code types, NO DB semantics) · wire surface (endpoint/event/webhook) → contracts (payloads REFERENCE structures via typeRef, never redefined) · a process → workflows · a behavior list → tests/requirements. Misclassifying a DTO as a model is a defect — pick the section by what the thing IS, not by its fields."
      },
      {
        "id": "60b91939-1655-41e7-a29f-0fdd89e649ef",
        "text": "STEP 1 — CHECK FIRST: query for an existing pebble on this topic (avoid duplicates); if a target you need to reference does not exist yet, create it first or note it for a second pass."
      },
      {
        "id": "3fd843c7-ce8c-459f-855a-b7bcc3f5dec5",
        "text": "STEP 2 — CREATE with real content: \"{PEBBLES_CLI}\" create <section> --title \"...\" [--kind K] [--content JSON]. Fields content needs a description + status per field (the CLI rejects otherwise); wire FKs via refKey when the target exists."
      },
      {
        "id": "6f1bac78-d44a-4d92-93cb-178749c07a1b",
        "text": "DESCRIPTIONS (every unit, every kind): write in TWO TIERS — (1) PLAIN LANGUAGE first, 1-3 sentences any stakeholder (product owner, QA, non-engineer) can read: what it is and how it works; (2) TECHNICAL last, a SEPARATE final paragraph: file:line, symbols, types, rules. A description states ONLY what the thing IS + its technical detail — NEVER an issue/bug/verdict (problems are FINDINGS, never descriptions). Be DETAILED: no stubs; an external/boundary node carries its FULL contract (direction + comm type + complete payload shape & requirements)."
      },
      {
        "id": "bcd9f7b0-f581-4a3c-8f2a-6b764aa97e39",
        "text": "Report: the created path + id, and any droppedRefs (links whose target did not resolve) with why."
      }
    ],
    "verify": [
      {
        "id": "6ecbbd2c-7717-4c8c-a1ea-6813c69dff28",
        "text": "The result shows ok:true and the returned path/id"
      },
      {
        "id": "32fdfe9a-56e8-4145-b02b-0a06962f9c56",
        "text": "droppedRefs is empty — or every drop is reported to the user with why"
      }
    ],
    "whenToUse": "Adding new spec: a model, requirement, workflow… The AI picks the right section and kind from your description."
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.740Z",
  "description": "Create a new pebble safely",
  "id": "1d2b6113-e760-43e3-86ea-b3e379a93f94",
